IMPORT prelude

-- Interpretation Act 1987 (New South Wales), Part 10 Application of State laws to coastal waters: sections 58 to 63. Part 9 (sections 54 to 57) is printed "(Repealed)".
-- The adjacent area and the territorial sea are fixed by Commonwealth Acts that are not among the sources, so whether a place falls within them is a plain input.

§ `Part 10 Application of State laws to coastal waters`

§§ `58 Definitions`

-- src:629 | adjacent area in respect of the State means the area the boundary of which was described under the heading referring to the State in Schedule 2 to the repealed Petroleum (Submerged Lands) Act 1967 of the Commonwealth, as in force immediately before the commencement of the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 of the Commonwealth.
@ref s 58 adjacent area (src:629)
GIVEN `the area has the boundary described under the heading referring to the State in Schedule 2 to the repealed Petroleum (Submerged Lands) Act 1967 of the Commonwealth, as in force immediately before the commencement of the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 58 the area is the adjacent area in respect of the State` MEANS
    `the area has the boundary described under the heading referring to the State in Schedule 2 to the repealed Petroleum (Submerged Lands) Act 1967 of the Commonwealth, as in force immediately before the commencement of the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 of the Commonwealth`

-- src:634 | territorial sea of Australia means the territorial sea of Australia within the limits referred to in section 4 (1) of the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 of the Commonwealth.
@ref s 58 territorial sea of Australia (src:634)
GIVEN `the sea is within the limits referred to in section 4 (1) of the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 58 the sea is the territorial sea of Australia` MEANS
    `the sea is within the limits referred to in section 4 (1) of the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 of the Commonwealth`

-- src:630 | coastal waters of the State means—
-- src:631 | (a) the part or parts of the territorial sea of Australia that is or are within the adjacent area in respect of the State, other than any part referred to in section 4 (2) of the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 of the Commonwealth, or
-- src:632 | (b) any sea that is on the landward side of any part of the territorial sea of Australia and is within the adjacent area in respect of the State, but is not within the limits of the State.
@ref s 58 coastal waters of the State (src:630-632)
GIVEN `it is a part of the territorial sea of Australia that is within the adjacent area in respect of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a part referred to in section 4 (2) of the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is sea on the landward side of a part of the territorial sea of Australia and within the adjacent area in respect of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is within the limits of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 58 the place is within the coastal waters of the State` MEANS
        (`it is a part of the territorial sea of Australia that is within the adjacent area in respect of the State` AND (NOT `it is a part referred to in section 4 (2) of the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 of the Commonwealth`))
     OR (`it is sea on the landward side of a part of the territorial sea of Australia and within the adjacent area in respect of the State` AND (NOT `it is within the limits of the State`))

-- src:633 | laws of the State means the laws (whether written or unwritten and whether substantive or procedural) that are from time to time in force in the State, but does not include laws of the Commonwealth.
@ref s 58 laws of the State (src:633)
GIVEN `the law is in force in the State from time to time, whether written or unwritten and whether substantive or procedural` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law is a law of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 58 the law is a law of the State` MEANS
    `the law is in force in the State from time to time, whether written or unwritten and whether substantive or procedural` AND (NOT `the law is a law of the Commonwealth`)

§§ `59 Application of laws of the State to coastal waters`

-- The places section 59 names.
DECLARE PlaceToWhichTheLawsOfTheStateApply IS ONE OF
    TheCoastalWatersOfTheState
    TheSeaBedAndSubsoilBeneathTheCoastalWatersOfTheState
    TheAirspaceAboveTheCoastalWatersOfTheState
    SomeOtherPlaceNotNamedInSection59

-- src:637 | The laws of the State apply in and in relation to—
-- src:638 | (a) the coastal waters of the State, and
-- src:639 | (b) the sea-bed and subsoil beneath, and the airspace above, the coastal waters of the State,
-- src:640 | as if the coastal waters of the State, as extending from time to time, were within the limits of the State.
@ref s 59 (src:637-640)
GIVEN place IS A PlaceToWhichTheLawsOfTheStateApply
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 59 the laws of the State apply in and in relation to the place as if the coastal waters of the State, as extending from time to time, were within the limits of the State` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN TheCoastalWatersOfTheState THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN TheSeaBedAndSubsoilBeneathTheCoastalWatersOfTheState THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN TheAirspaceAboveTheCoastalWatersOfTheState THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN SomeOtherPlaceNotNamedInSection59 THEN NOTHING

§§ `60 Laws with specific application not to apply`

-- src:643 | (1) Nothing in this Part renders a provision of the laws of the State applicable in a particular place—
-- src:644 | (a) in so far as the provision is incapable of applying in or in relation to that place,
-- src:645 | (b) if those laws expressly provide that the provision does not extend or apply in or in relation to that place, or
-- src:646 | (c) if those laws expressly provide that the provision applies only in a specified locality in the State that does not include that place.
@ref s 60(1) (src:643-646)
GIVEN `the provision is incapable of applying in or in relation to that place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the laws of the State expressly provide that the provision does not extend or apply in or in relation to that place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the laws of the State expressly provide that the provision applies only in a specified locality in the State that does not include that place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60(1) Part 10 renders the provision of the laws of the State applicable in the place` MEANS
    IF `the provision is incapable of applying in or in relation to that place` OR `the laws of the State expressly provide that the provision does not extend or apply in or in relation to that place` OR `the laws of the State expressly provide that the provision applies only in a specified locality in the State that does not include that place`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:647 | (2) A provision of the laws of the State shall not be taken to be a provision to which subsection (1) applies merely because it is limited in its application to acts, matters and things within the territorial or adjacent waters (however described) of the State.
@ref s 60(2) (src:647)
GIVEN `the provision is limited in its application to acts, matters and things within the territorial or adjacent waters (however described) of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60(2) the provision is taken to be a provision to which section 60(1) applies merely because of that limit` MEANS
    IF `the provision is limited in its application to acts, matters and things within the territorial or adjacent waters (however described) of the State` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `61 Extent of jurisdiction in relation to coastal waters`

-- src:650 | (1) All persons who have functions conferred or imposed on them by law for the purposes of or in connection with a provision of the laws of the State shall have and may exercise all or any of those functions for the purposes of or in connection with that provision, as applying by virtue of this Part, as if the coastal waters of the State, as extending from time to time, were within the limits of the State.
@ref s 61(1) (src:650)
GIVEN `the person has functions conferred or imposed on the person by law for the purposes of or in connection with a provision of the laws of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61(1) the person has and may exercise the functions in connection with the provision, as applying by virtue of Part 10, as if the coastal waters of the State were within the limits of the State` MEANS
    IF `the person has functions conferred or imposed on the person by law for the purposes of or in connection with a provision of the laws of the State` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:651 | (2) The several courts of the State are invested with jurisdiction in all matters arising under the provisions of the laws of the State, as applying by virtue of this Part, as if the coastal waters of the State, as extending from time to time, were within the limits of the State.
@ref s 61(2) (src:651)
GIVEN `the matter arises under a provision of the laws of the State, as applying by virtue of Part 10` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61(2) the courts of the State are invested with jurisdiction in the matter` MEANS
    IF `the matter arises under a provision of the laws of the State, as applying by virtue of Part 10` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `62 Constitutional basis`

-- src:654 | In addition to any other power under which the provisions of this Part may be enacted, the provisions of this Part are enacted under the legislative power of Parliament as extended by section 5 of the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 of the Commonwealth.
@ref s 62 (src:654)
GIVEN `it is a provision of Part 10` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62 the provision is enacted under the legislative power of Parliament as extended by section 5 of the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 of the Commonwealth, in addition to any other power under which it may be enacted` MEANS
    IF `it is a provision of Part 10` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `63 Saving`

-- src:657 | Nothing in this Part limits any other law that provides for the application of the laws of the State, or any part of those laws, beyond the limits of the State.
@ref s 63 (src:657)
GIVEN `it is another law that provides for the application of the laws of the State, or any part of those laws, beyond the limits of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 63 Part 10 limits the other law` MEANS
    IF `it is another law that provides for the application of the laws of the State, or any part of those laws, beyond the limits of the State` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Tests: Part 10`

#ASSERT `s 58 the area is the adjacent area in respect of the State` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 58 the area is the adjacent area in respect of the State` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 58 the sea is the territorial sea of Australia` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 58 the sea is the territorial sea of Australia` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- paragraph (a): territorial sea within the adjacent area, other than a part referred to in section 4(2)
#ASSERT `s 58 the place is within the coastal waters of the State` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 58 the place is within the coastal waters of the State` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- paragraph (b): sea on the landward side, within the adjacent area, but not within the limits of the State
#ASSERT `s 58 the place is within the coastal waters of the State` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 58 the place is within the coastal waters of the State` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 58 the place is within the coastal waters of the State` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 58 the law is a law of the State` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 58 the law is a law of the State` TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 58 the law is a law of the State` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 59 the laws of the State apply in and in relation to the place as if the coastal waters of the State, as extending from time to time, were within the limits of the State` TheCoastalWatersOfTheState EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 59 the laws of the State apply in and in relation to the place as if the coastal waters of the State, as extending from time to time, were within the limits of the State` TheSeaBedAndSubsoilBeneathTheCoastalWatersOfTheState EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 59 the laws of the State apply in and in relation to the place as if the coastal waters of the State, as extending from time to time, were within the limits of the State` TheAirspaceAboveTheCoastalWatersOfTheState EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 59 the laws of the State apply in and in relation to the place as if the coastal waters of the State, as extending from time to time, were within the limits of the State` SomeOtherPlaceNotNamedInSection59 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 60(1) Part 10 renders the provision of the laws of the State applicable in the place` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 60(1) Part 10 renders the provision of the laws of the State applicable in the place` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 60(1) Part 10 renders the provision of the laws of the State applicable in the place` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 60(1) Part 10 renders the provision of the laws of the State applicable in the place` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 60(2) the provision is taken to be a provision to which section 60(1) applies merely because of that limit` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 60(2) the provision is taken to be a provision to which section 60(1) applies merely because of that limit` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 61(1) the person has and may exercise the functions in connection with the provision, as applying by virtue of Part 10, as if the coastal waters of the State were within the limits of the State` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 61(1) the person has and may exercise the functions in connection with the provision, as applying by virtue of Part 10, as if the coastal waters of the State were within the limits of the State` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 61(2) the courts of the State are invested with jurisdiction in the matter` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 61(2) the courts of the State are invested with jurisdiction in the matter` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 62 the provision is enacted under the legislative power of Parliament as extended by section 5 of the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 of the Commonwealth, in addition to any other power under which it may be enacted` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62 the provision is enacted under the legislative power of Parliament as extended by section 5 of the Coastal Waters (State Powers) Act 1980 of the Commonwealth, in addition to any other power under which it may be enacted` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 63 Part 10 limits the other law` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63 Part 10 limits the other law` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
